      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily with meals. This order is about 5 times that. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, if you meant a lower dose (this isn't a standard tablet strength, so 500 mg may fit better)\n- **500 mg PO twice or three times daily**, a common starting or maintenance regimen\n\nTell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 4250 mg is deliberate, and I'll enter the order."
      }
