     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about 5 times the maximum recommended daily dose, and I know of no indication that would justify it. A single 4,250 mg dose is in the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't make it safe, and I'd be putting a potentially harmful order in front of nurses and pharmacists.\n\nHere are some other ways to proceed:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can enter that right now.\n- **Consult pharmacy or endocrinology.** If you're considering something unusual, they can review it with you first.\n- **Use your institution's override pathway.** If you still want this dose after that review, it should go through a process with direct pharmacist verification, not through me.\n\nIf a different dose or drug was intended, tell me and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
